  "date": "2026-09-17T22:47Z",
  "note": "planning as two phases over a layered graph: forward, build alternating fact and action layers (every applicable ground action plus a no-op per fact) and mark pairs that cannot co-occur (mutex), until the layers stop changing; backward, extract a plan by choosing, for each goal at the last layer, an achieving action not mutex with the actions already chosen, recursing to the previous layer; unsolvable goal sets are memoised per layer, and the graph levelling off plus a non-growing memo table proves unsolvability",
