   "human_interpretation": "UNKNOWN",
   "mechanism": "two actions at a layer are mutex if one deletes a precondition or effect of the other (interference) or if their preconditions are mutex (competing needs); two facts at a layer are mutex if every pair of their achievers is mutex; the relation is a per-layer bit vector (bvec_len) read by are_mutex; during extraction, choosing an action marks every action mutex with it as unavailable (mark_exclusive) and unmarks on backtrack",
   "input": "the layer's actions and their precondition/effect/delete lists",
   "output": "a symmetric relation per layer",
   "state": "bit vectors",
   "update": "per layer",
   "assumptions": [
    "binary exclusion captures most of what makes goal sets unachievable; higher-order exclusions are left to the search"
   ],
